# Guardrails ({{project_name}})

<!-- Owned by the project; /sync never touches it. Only the "Signs" section is sent to the local worker with every
     request, so keep it short (20 signs at most). This file is advice: a rule that must never be broken belongs in
     a gate or in [scope] protected of .harness/harness.toml, and is only pointed to here. -->

## Enforced (not advice)
- Protected and generated paths: `[scope] protected` in `.harness/harness.toml`. An attempt that changes one fails and
  goes back to the worker; nothing is reverted automatically, so if the ladder runs out Claude reverts it on the task branch.
- Files outside a task's "Files in scope": same treatment by the scope guard. A task without that section is not
  scope-checked (the review brief says "scope unknown").
- Fast and full gates: `[gates]` in `.harness/harness.toml`. A failing gate sends the task back to the worker; nothing
  is committed until they pass.
- Commands the worker may run: the gate commands (as written or with extra arguments) plus what `.claude/settings.json`
  allows; never `git`. File tools: Read, Edit, Write, Glob, Grep.

